{:schema 1
 :name "flexiarg directive ontology"
 :purpose
 "The machine-readable half of README-flexiarg.md, and the ingest whitelist.

  A directive reaches the store ONLY if it is :standard here. Anything else is
  REPORTED as an anomaly and not ingested -- unknown labels cannot be assigned
  semantics, and a parser that guesses is how a library stops meaning what its
  authors wrote (README-flexiarg §8).

  Standardising a directive is an editorial act in THIS FILE, reviewable in one
  diff. It is not a code change, and it is not automatic.

  Founded 2026-08-17 by claude-2 at Joe's direction, from a census of all 1151
  library files: 80 distinct directives, 11 parsed, 69 dropped in silence.
  Statuses:
    :standard      ingested; semantics agreed and written in README-flexiarg
    :variant-of    a spelling of a standard directive; migrate, do not ingest
    :split         conflates two standard relations; migrate PER EDGE
    :not-an-edge   looks structural, is not -- do not admit to the pattern graph
    :candidate     real usage, semantics NOT yet ruled; read before standardising
    :family-scoped bespoke payload for one family; never global
    :unreviewed    counted, not yet read"
